  1. THE CEILING — what blocking makes reachable at all
     0 days 96.197%  ->  unbounded 96.816%   total span 0.619 pts
     narrowest window within 0.1 pts of the maximum: +/-7 (96.720%)
     The window buys almost nothing: 0.619 points separate no window
     at all from an unbounded one. Blocking on date is not what makes this
     dataset retrievable.

  2. RANKING — what widening costs
     match     0 days 96.001%  ->  unbounded 94.787%   (-1.214 pts)
     precision 0 days 99.682%  ->  unbounded 97.599%   (-2.084 pts)
     pool      0 days 6.69  ->  unbounded 36.72 candidates per query
     Widening the window makes retrieval WORSE, not better. The extra
     candidates it admits are overwhelmingly wrong ones, and every one of
     them is another chance for cosine to rank a decoy first.

  3. IS +/-7 ON A PLATEAU OR AN EDGE?
     ceiling at +/-7                        96.720%
     lost by narrowing to +/-3              0.090 pts
     gained by widening to +/-30            0.080 pts
     match rate given up by widening to +/-30  0.369 pts
     PLATEAU. Neither halving nor quadrupling the window moves the ceiling
     by a quarter of a point. +/-7 is not a tuned value and nothing here
     depends on it being 7. A deployment with slower settlement can widen
     it safely, at a small and measurable cost in ranking precision.

  4. ASYMMETRIC — settlement delay runs in one direction
     ledger-before only, 7      ceiling  96.603% (-0.116)  match  95.519% (+0.150)  pool  10.39 (-3.69)
     statement-before only, 7   ceiling  96.314% (-0.406)  match  95.568% (+0.200)  pool  10.38 (-3.70)
     ledger-before only, 30     ceiling  96.653% (-0.146)  match  95.163% (+0.163)  pool  15.44 (-8.69)
     statement-before only, 30  ceiling  96.344% (-0.456)  match  95.272% (+0.273)  pool  15.38 (-8.75)
     One-sided at 7 costs 0.116 points of ceiling against the symmetric window while
     roughly halving the pool. Which side matters more is a property of the
     data's own timing, printed as ground truth at the top of this section.

